{"id":"beats-274e84","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-d101a780-5f51-4fb0-9127-6afde98103c3","text":"## Implementation\n\nAdded keyboard shortcuts to the issue detail view.\n\n### Shortcuts (when viewing an issue, no input focused)\n- **`S`** — open status popover\n- **`L`** — open labels popover\n- **`E`** — open estimate popover\n- **`1`** — set Backlog, **`2`** — Planned, **`3`** — In Progress, **`4`** — Blocked, **`5`** — Done\n- **`j`** / **`→`** — next issue, **`k`** / **`←`** — previous issue\n- **`Esc`** — close popover → close editing → close issue (cascading)\n\n### Global shortcuts (from App.tsx, already existed)\n- **`Cmd+K`** — command palette\n- **`C`** — new issue\n\n### Notes\n- Shortcuts are disabled when typing in an input/textarea\n- Shortcuts are disabled when a popover is already open (except Esc)\n- Number keys fire saveDraft directly for instant status change\n\n### Files changed\n- `web/src/components/IssueDetail/IssueDetail.tsx` — extended keydown handler"},"created_at":"2026-05-19T08:20:05.216051Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-274e84","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-05-19T08:20:05.244911Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-8d0a00","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Cross-link issues","description":"When we detect an issue pattern `prefix-id` either in description or comments, we should automatically render a link to that issue. Additionally, when issues are related, we see a \"Related issues\" section in the aside of the issue details view, but those issues are also not links (even though colored blue).","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-19T10:09:00.003851Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-7d6c67","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Copy issue ID","description":"We should have a way to quickly copy an issue ID from both the issue index view, and the issue details view. bonus points if there was a shortcut that worked in both views","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-19T10:10:09.839102Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-2990b5","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Sorting issues for prioritization","description":"It would be great if we could re-order issues in the issues index view to prioritize.","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-19T10:11:18.465373Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-a3e1c7","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"Add sort and filter UI to the backlog tab bar.\n\n## Filter By\n\n- Label (multi-select)\n- Status (multi-select, in addition to tab-based filtering)\n- Assignee\n- Has estimate / no estimate\n\n## Sort By\n\n- Created date (default)\n- Updated date\n- Estimate (high to low)\n- Title (alphabetical)\n- Priority\n\n## Design\n\n- Filter icon button in the tab bar opens a dropdown with filter options\n- Active filters shown as removable chips\n- Sort dropdown next to the filter button\n- Persist sort/filter preferences in localStorage"},"created_at":"2026-05-19T10:11:50.485968Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-8e74b1","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-05-19T10:15:37.640805Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-8e74b1","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-19T10:15:37.670484Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"beats-8e74b1","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-878586bc-ecbd-40de-b0a0-4a4f37394600","text":"## Implementation\n\nAdded inline issue creation from the backlog status group headers.\n\n### How it works\n- Each status group header now has a `+` button on the right\n- Clicking it opens an inline input row at the top of that group\n- Type a title and press Enter to create — the issue gets the group's status\n- Esc or blur cancels\n- After creation, the input stays open for quick batch entry\n- If status isn't BACKLOG, a follow-up UPDATE draft sets the correct status\n\n### Files changed\n- `web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx` — added inline creation state, handler, and UI"},"created_at":"2026-05-19T10:21:56.439688Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
